WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.147
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 12. Topic: HKDSE 2026 · Paper 1 · Q12. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:22.894
The straight line L passes through the point (minus 10,11). The slope of L is minus 2. (a) Find the equation of L.

3
00:00:23.054 --> 00:00:35.258
(b) The coordinates of the points H and K are (2,5) and (minus 4,-7) respectively. Let P be a point lying on L such that P is equidistant from H and K.

4
00:00:35.418 --> 00:00:49.072
(i) Find the coordinates of P. (ii) Let Q be a point such that HPKQ is a quadrilateral, where HP equals HQ equals KQ. Find the area of the quadrilateral HPKQ.

5
00:00:49.492 --> 00:00:51.364
Step 1.

6
00:00:51.524 --> 00:00:58.080
Key rule: Point-Slope Form. y-y sub 1 equals m(x-x sub 1).

7
00:00:58.240 --> 00:01:08.430
Using (minus 10,11) and slope minus 2 gives y minus 11 equals minus 2(x plus 10), that is y equals minus 2x minus 9.

8
00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:15.679
Step 1 times Equation of L Using the point–slope form with point (minus 10,11) and slope minus 2.

9
00:01:15.839 --> 00:01:26.796
y minus 11 equals minus 2(x plus 10) which gives y equals minus 2x minus 9 💡 Notice the slope is negative, so the line goes steeply down to the right.

10
00:01:27.216 --> 00:01:29.175
Step 2.

11
00:01:29.335 --> 00:01:38.838
Key rule: Perpendicular Bisector from Equidistance. PH squared equals PK squared tends to perpendicular bisector of HK.

12
00:01:38.998 --> 00:01:48.988
Expanding and cancelling x squared plus y squared leaves 12x plus 24y equals minus 36, i.e. x plus 2y equals minus 3.

13
00:01:49.148 --> 00:01:57.637
Step 2 times Equidistance condition Let P equals (x, y). From PH squared equals PK squared.

14
00:01:57.797 --> 00:02:09.474
(x minus 2) squared plus (y minus 5) squared equals (x plus 4) squared plus (y plus 7) squared Expanding and cancelling x squared plus y squared.

15
00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:23.715
minus 4x minus 10y plus 29 equals 8x plus 14y plus 65 12x plus 24y equals minus 36 which gives x plus 2y equals minus 3 This is the perpendicular bisector of HK.

16
00:02:24.135 --> 00:02:26.154
Step 3.

17
00:02:26.314 --> 00:02:34.299
Step 3 times Intersect with L Substitute y equals minus 2x minus 9 into x plus 2y equals minus 3.

18
00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:49.932
x plus 2(minus 2x minus 9) equals minus 3 minus 3x minus 18 equals minus 3 which gives x equals minus 5 y equals minus 2(minus 5)-9 equals 1 So P equals (minus 5, 1).

19
00:02:50.092 --> 00:02:56.933
Check: PH squared equals 49 plus 16 equals 65 equals PK squared ✓.

20
00:02:57.353 --> 00:02:59.300
Step 4.

21
00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:10.547
Step 4 times Locate Q Q is also at distance HP equals the square root of 65 from both H and K, so Q also lies on x plus 2y equals minus 3.

22
00:03:10.707 --> 00:03:20.010
Let Q equals (x, y) with x equals minus 3 minus 2y. From HQ squared equals 65.

23
00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:35.867
(minus 5 minus 2y) squared plus (y minus 5) squared equals 65 5y squared plus 10y plus 50 equals 65 y squared plus 2y minus 3 equals 0 which gives (y plus 3)(y minus 1).

24
00:03:36.027 --> 00:03:47.382
equals 0 y equals 1 gives Q equals P (rejected); y equals minus 3 gives x equals 3. So Q equals (3, minus 3).

25
00:03:47.802 --> 00:03:49.891
Step 5.

26
00:03:50.051 --> 00:03:57.055
Key rule: Area of a Rhombus. area equals 1 over 2 d sub 1 d sub 2.

27
00:03:57.215 --> 00:04:05.188
The diagonals are HK equals 6 the square root of 5 and PQ equals 4 the square root of 5, so the area is 60.

28
00:04:05.348 --> 00:04:17.059
Step 5 times Area (rhombus shortcut) All four sides equal the square root of 65, so HPKQ is a rhombus; its diagonals HK and PQ are perpendicular.

29
00:04:17.219 --> 00:04:23.047
HK equals the square root of 6 squared plus 12 squared equals 65.

30
00:04:23.207 --> 00:04:38.550
PQ equals the square root of 8 squared plus 4 squared equals 45 Area equals 12 times HK times PQ equals 12(65)(45) equals 60 Shoelace check with (2,5),(minus 5,1).

31
00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:49.407
(minus 4,-7),(3,-3) gives 12 (64 minus (minus 56)) equals 12(120) equals 60 ✓.

32
00:04:49.827 --> 00:05:01.185
So the answer is: s: (a) y equals minus 2x minus 9 (b)(i) P equals (minus 5, 1) (b)(ii) Area equals 60.

33
00:05:01.605 --> 00:05:10.613
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 12. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
